IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Television and Radio Licensing) (Revocation) Regulations 2012 (S 548/2012), made under s 66 of the Act by the Media Development Authority of Singapore with the Minister's approval.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-television-and-radio-licensing-revocation-regulations-2012/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S548-2012.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited).
-- Made 30 October 2012; "First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 31st October 2012 at 5.00 pm" (the same day and hour as S 549/2012); paragraph 1: it "shall be deemed to have come into operation on 1st January 2011".
-- TWO TIME AXES (design instruction of 2026-11-03): the version takes effect on 1 January 2011 (valid time) and was published on 31 October 2012 (rule-version time); `sgba-versions.l4` reads the version table on a conduct day and a reading day.
-- The 5.00 pm is not kept (a reading day is a date). Whether a retrospective revocation is valid, and what a court would do with conduct already past, is not addressed.

§ `Regulation 1: commencement, as the version row`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 31st October 2012 at 5.00 pm.
-- src:28 | Citation and commencement
-- src:29 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Broadcasting (Television
-- src:30 | and Radio Licensing) (Revocation) Regulations 2012 and shall be
-- src:31 | deemed to have come into operation on 1st January 2011.
@ref S 548/2012 publication line and reg 1 (citation and commencement) (src:3-31)
`Rg 1 as revoked by S 548/2012` MEANS
    `Rg 1 version` WITH `source` IS "S 548/2012, made 30 October 2012, first published 31 October 2012 at 5.00 pm, deemed in operation from 1 January 2011"
                      , `the text read` IS "revoked by S 548/2012"
                      , `takes effect on` IS (Date 1 1 2011)
                      , `published on` IS (Date 31 10 2012)
                      , `the Regulations are in force` IS FALSE

§ `Regulation 2: revocation and savings`

-- src:33 | Revocation and savings
-- src:34 | 2.—(1) The Broadcasting (Television and Radio Licensing)
-- src:35 | Regulations (Rg 1) (referred to in these Regulations as the revoked
-- src:36 | Regulations) are revoked.
@ref reg 2(1): the Regulations (Rg 1) are revoked (src:33-36)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 548 reg 2(1) the revoking Regulations take effect on or before the day of the conduct` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011)

-- src:37 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the revoked Regulations shall
-- src:38 | continue to apply to and in relation to —
-- src:39 | (a) every licence granted under section 20(1) of the Act, in respect
-- src:40 | of any broadcast television receiver or broadcast sound
-- src:41 | receiver, for any period before 1st January 2011;
@ref reg 2(2)(a): the revoked Regulations continue to apply to every licence granted under s 20(1) for a receiver, for any period before 1 January 2011 (src:37-41)
GIVEN `the licence was granted under section 20(1) of the Act in respect of a broadcast television receiver or a broadcast sound receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the period the licence is for` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 548 reg 2(2)(a) the revoked Regulations continue to apply to the licence for that day` MEANS
    `the licence was granted under section 20(1) of the Act in respect of a broadcast television receiver or a broadcast sound receiver` AND `a day in the period the licence is for` AT MOST (Date 31 12 2010)

-- src:42 | (b) every broadcast television receiver or broadcast sound
-- src:43 | receiver in respect of which any licence referred to in
-- src:44 | sub-paragraph (a) has been granted, in respect of any matter
-- src:45 | S 548/2012 2
-- src:47 | concerning that broadcast television receiver or broadcast
-- src:48 | sound receiver which occurred before 1st January 2011; and
@ref reg 2(2)(b): the revoked Regulations continue to apply to every such receiver in respect of any matter which occurred before 1 January 2011 (src:42-48)
GIVEN `a licence referred to in sub-paragraph (a) has been granted in respect of the receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the matter concerning the receiver occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 548 reg 2(2)(b) the revoked Regulations continue to apply to the receiver for that matter` MEANS
    `a licence referred to in sub-paragraph (a) has been granted in respect of the receiver` AND `the day the matter concerning the receiver occurred` AT MOST (Date 31 12 2010)

-- src:49 | (c) every person to whom any licence referred to in
-- src:50 | sub-paragraph (a) has been granted, in respect of any thing
-- src:51 | which he is required, before 1st January 2011, to do under
-- src:52 | the revoked Regulations,
-- src:53 | as if these Regulations had not been made.
@ref reg 2(2)(c): the revoked Regulations continue to apply to every person to whom such a licence was granted, in respect of any thing required to be done before 1 January 2011 (src:49-53)
GIVEN `a licence referred to in sub-paragraph (a) has been granted to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day by which the person was required to do the thing under the revoked Regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 548 reg 2(2)(c) the revoked Regulations continue to apply to the person for that thing` MEANS
    `a licence referred to in sub-paragraph (a) has been granted to the person` AND `the day by which the person was required to do the thing under the revoked Regulations` AT MOST (Date 31 12 2010)

-- src:54 | (3) Any fee for the grant or renewal of a licence, and any additional
-- src:55 | fee for the variation of a licence, that has been paid in advance under
-- src:56 | regulation 5 of the revoked Regulations, for any period commencing on
-- src:57 | or after 1st January 2011, shall be refunded to the licensee in full.
@ref reg 2(3): any fee paid in advance under reg 5 of the revoked Regulations for a period commencing on or after 1 January 2011 is refunded in full (src:54-57)
GIVEN `a fee for the grant or renewal of a licence, or an additional fee for the variation of a licence, was paid in advance under regulation 5 of the revoked Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the period for which the fee was paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 548 reg 2(3) the fee is to be refunded to the licensee in full` MEANS
    `a fee for the grant or renewal of a licence, or an additional fee for the variation of a licence, was paid in advance under regulation 5 of the revoked Regulations` AND `the first day of the period for which the fee was paid` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011)
